# Colorado Parks and Wildlife (CPW) publishes where its species live as one ArcGIS Online feature
# service with 313 layers, one for each species and kind of area. These fields are written by
# hand. The layers have names only, so the fields split each name into the species and the kind.

extend type Query {
	"""
	The wildlife areas mapped by Colorado Parks and Wildlife (CPW) that contain a point in Colorado: the ranges of
	species such as black bears, mountain lions, elk and rattlesnakes, and the human conflict areas where bears and
	mountain lions meet people. These are range maps drawn by the state's biologists. The sightings that people
	report are in the inat fields. Use it to answer whether a place, such as an owner's home or a trailhead, lies where
	bears, mountain lions or rattlesnakes live, which matters for walking a dog or letting a cat outside.
	Without species, the call asks all 313 layers of the service, which takes a few seconds and an answer of about
	80 KB from CPW, and usually finds about 60 areas. Pass species to ask only the matching layers.
	"""
	cpwWildlifeAt(
		"The latitude of the point, for example 40.015 for Boulder or 39.739 for downtown Denver."
		latitude: Float!
		"The longitude of the point, west of Greenwich, so negative in Colorado, for example -105.2705 for Boulder."
		longitude: Float!
		"Text that the species or the layer name contains, in upper or lower case, for example bear, mountain lion, rattlesnake or Human Conflict. Leave it out to ask every layer."
		species: String
	): [CpwWildlifeArea!]!

	"""
	The 313 layers of the Colorado Parks and Wildlife species data, one for each species and kind of area, such as
	Black Bear Human Conflict Area, Elk Winter Range or Bald Eagle Nest Sites, sorted by species. Use it to find
	which species and kinds of area CPW maps in Colorado.
	"""
	cpwWildlifeLayers(
		"Text that the species or the layer name contains, in upper or lower case, for example bear or Winter Range. Leave it out for every layer."
		species: String
	): [CpwWildlifeLayer!]!
}

"""
An area mapped by Colorado Parks and Wildlife that contains the point a query asked about, such as the human
conflict area of black bears.
"""
type CpwWildlifeArea {
	"The species or group of species, for example Black Bear, Mountain Lion or Prairie Rattlesnake And Western Rattlesnake."
	species: String!
	"""
	The kind of area, for example Human Conflict Area, Overall Range, Winter Range, Migration Corridors or
	Breeding Range. Null when the layer name does not end with a known kind.
	"""
	kind: String
	"The name of the CPW layer, for example Black Bear Human Conflict Area."
	layerName: String!
	"The id of the layer in the CPW service."
	layerId: Int!
	"The code CPW gives the area within its layer, for example BBHCA for a black bear human conflict area. Null for some layers, such as Lynx Habitat."
	activityCode: String
}

"A layer of the Colorado Parks and Wildlife species data, for one species and one kind of area."
type CpwWildlifeLayer {
	"The id of the layer in the CPW service."
	layerId: Int!
	"The name of the layer, for example Mountain Lion Human Conflict Area."
	layerName: String!
	"The species or group of species, for example Mountain Lion."
	species: String!
	"The kind of area, for example Human Conflict Area or Overall Range. Null when the layer name does not end with a known kind."
	kind: String
}
